WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit
6: Describing People and Things.

2
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.300
Welcome to Unit 6!

3
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.660
In this unit you will learn how to describe people and things.

4
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:18.480
You will learn words for what a person is like on
the inside — such as kind, honest and friendly —

5
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:24.240
and words for what things are like on the
outside — such as rough, tough and smooth.

6
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:32.080
You will describe your favourite people, compare
two things, and tell true stories about the past.

7
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.610
By the end, you will be ready to
enjoy this unit's story about Nadia,

8
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:42.140
a new girl who learns that carrying
kindness makes everyone feel welcome.

9
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:48.540
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:55.780
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use describing
words (adjectives) to talk about people and things.

11
00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.780
you will also describe your favourite
person and say what makes them special.

12
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.700
you will also compare two people or things,
using words like kinder and rougher than.

13
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.660
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.520
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
kind, friendly, honest, kindness, care, busy.

15
00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:22.880
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.460
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:32.200
The reading sequence includes My Cousin Ishmael and Two Roads.

18
00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:33.840
Read actively.

19
00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:39.120
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.200
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:47.840
The first language focus is The Past Simple Tense.

22
00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.420
We use the past simple to talk
about things that already happened.

23
00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:58.600
It helps us tell stories and describe what people
did — like Hannah, who helped the boy who fell.

24
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:06.580
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:13.260
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1 — Describe Your Favourite Person.

26
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:18.520
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.720
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.640
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.400
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:35.380
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:38.400
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:44.760
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
